  "details": "So many time I will be in a public or between friends where we want to add each other on discord or want to send a funny image/ meme between the group and you have to say \"What's your discord\" or \"X can send it to you\". What if we could just actively reach out to people on discord via VRChat?\n\nIt would be nice to be able to add discord friends directly within VRChat to help make the whole \"What's your discord\" chat more seamless. It would be just be an additional option with people that you get where you can send a discord friend request directly as part of their profile page.\n\nThere could be multiple options in the privacy/ safety settings for this to allow different levels of access to your discord:\n\n1. Public - Allows people to add you on discord regardless who you are (Could be limited to same instance or just overall public )\n\n2. Friends Only - Only people on your VRChat friends list can send you a friend request on discord.\n\n3. Private - Prevents anyone from seeing your discord\n\nThis is a suggestion came from my friend SomethingSpicy when she asked why would you want to link your VRChat and Discord accounts so shout out to them!",
